# Rust Implementation & Testing

## Implementation loop

```text
READ SPEC → AUDIT REPO → IDENTIFY CONTRACT → IMPLEMENT MINIMAL SCOPE
→ TEST → AUDIT → REPORT
```

Do not: speculative abstractions, future modules early, unused extension points,
undocumented behavior, silent API broadening, convenience dependencies.

Prefer the smallest implementation that fully satisfies the frozen contract.

## Dependencies

Justify every crate. Prefer std. Check necessity, maintenance, security,
determinism, license, compile cost, and scope before adding.

## API discipline

Do not accidentally freeze public APIs. Unspecified surfaces stay internal or
are marked provisional. Do not infer CLI / REST / GraphQL / SDK / DSL /
serialization / plugin / bindings unless authorized by specification.

## Error semantics

Do not collapse distinct classes. A failed economic action ≠ engine error.
An invariant violation ≠ engine error. A harness expectation mismatch ≠
economic truth violation.

## Testing

Every behavior change needs tests covering happy path, boundaries, invalid
input, error semantics, determinism, numeric safety, transitions, and
regression where relevant. Assert exact authoritative outcomes — not
incidental implementation details when the spec defines observable semantics.

## Documentation truthfulness

Use explicit status (`DRAFT`, `READY_FOR_REVIEW`, `FROZEN`,
`IMPLEMENTATION_BLOCKED`, `IMPLEMENTED`, `PASS`, `PARTIAL`, `NOT_IMPLEMENTED`).
Never claim implemented / production-ready / complete without evidence.

## Required implementation report

```text
TASK:
STATUS:
SPECIFICATION:
SPECIFICATION_COMPLIANCE:
FILES_CHANGED:
DEPENDENCIES_ADDED:
TESTS:
CI:
DETERMINISM:
NUMERIC_SAFETY:
SCOPE_CREEP:
KNOWN_LIMITATIONS:
OPEN_DECISIONS:
REMAINING_BLOCKERS:
COMMIT:
NEXT:
```

Reports must be truthful.

## Final principle

```text
NO DRIFT. NO HIDDEN SEMANTICS. NO UNAUTHORIZED IMPLEMENTATION.
NO NON-DETERMINISTIC ECONOMIC TRUTH. NO LLM ECONOMIC AUTHORITY.
NO SPECIFICATION BY ACCIDENTAL CODE. NO PASS WITHOUT EVIDENCE.
```
